body: "# W7 touring-bindings Fusion — COMPLETE\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-15\n**Wave**: W7 (touring-bindings Fusion) of touring-premium-refactor-2026\n**Status**: COMPLETE — all 7 crates fused, no exclusion\n**Workspace state**: GREEN (cargo check --workspace 0 errors)\n\n## Result\n\nSeven language-binding crates fused into a single `touring-bindings` crate;\nthe originals reduced to one-file re-export shims.\n\n| Source crate | LOC | Fate |\n|---|---|---|\n| touring-python | 3456 | touring-bindings/src/python/ |\n| touring-wasm | 2666 | touring-bindings/src/wasm/ |\n| touring-capnp-server | 1513 | touring-bindings/src/capnp/ |\n| touring-web | 3539 | touring-bindings/src/web/ |\n| touring-web-server | 1705 | touring-bindings/src/web/server/ |\n| touring-desktop-ui | 1189 | touring-bindings/src/desktop/ |\n| touring-geopostgis | 435 | touring-bindings/src/postgis/ |\n| touring-bindings (fused) | 14651 | new crate, 84 files |\n\n## Cycle analysis — all 7 fuse, NO exclusion\n\nUnlike W5 (excluded touring-index) and W6 (excluded touring-cortex), W7\nfuses all 7 crates. Verified cycle-safe: the 7 crates depend only on\n{foundation, simd, touring-intelligence, touring-code}; none depends on\nhooks/server/cortex/generator. touring-wasm is consumed by\nhooks/generator/cortex/server and touring-capnp-server by hooks, but this\nforms a clean DAG (hooks -> touring-bindings -> {low layers}, no back-edge).\n\n## Validation Gates\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| cargo check --workspace | 0 errors |\n| cargo check -p touring-bindings (default, empty features) | 0 errors |\n| cargo test -p touring-bindings (bind-capnp,bind-web,bind-postgis) | 53 PASS + 1 doctest, 0 failed |\n| cargo clippy -p touring-bindings + 7 shims | 0 errors (51 style warnings -> 11 after --fix) |\n| consumer compile (hooks/generator/cortex/server) | 0 errors |\n| touring wiring cycles --min-depth 2 | 2 / depth 621 (unchanged) |\n\n## Features\n\n`default = []` (all opt-in). 6 public bind-* features: bind-python,\nbind-wasm, bind-capnp, bind-web, bind-desktop, bind-postgis. Tier-free\nbuilds skip pyo3/wasm-bindgen/tauri/axum compile cost.\n\n## Special details preserved\n\n- touring-python shim keeps `[lib] name = \"claude_learning_kernel\"` +\n  `crate-type = [\"cdylib\",\"rlib\"]` (PyO3 extension module).\n- touring-web-server shim keeps its `[[bin]]` — main.rs delegates to\n  `touring_bindings::web::server::run`; `tokio` re-added for `#[tokio::main]`.\n- touring-wasm / touring-capnp-server shims default-enable bind-wasm /\n  bind-capnp (consumers expect the symbols unconditionally).\n\n## Pre-existing breakage (NOT W7 regressions)\n\n- `cargo test --features bind-python` fails at link (libpython) — inherent\n  to PyO3 extension-module crates; the crate compiles, only the test binary\n  fails to link. PyO3 is tested via maturin/pytest. Deferred to W11.\n- bind-wasm / bind-desktop need wasm32 / Tauri targets — host-checked only.\n- 11 residual clippy style warnings in fused code (origin crates lacked\n  workspace lints). Deferred to W11.\n\n## Bugs fixed during execution\n\n- w7 rewriter skipped examples/ and doc-comment scopes: `crate::web::snapshots`\n  needed `crate::web::server::snapshots` (nested submodule); 4\n  `touring_capnp_server::` refs in examples/; 21 `touring_<crate>::` refs in\n  src/ doc-comments. 25 refs corrected + 1 manual import fix.\n- touring-web-server shim main.rs needed `tokio` dependency for `#[tokio::main]`.\n\n## Files\n\n```\ncrates/touring-bindings/               NEW — 14651 LOC, 84 files, 6 modules\ncrates/touring-{python,wasm,capnp-server,web,web-server,desktop-ui,geopostgis}/\n                                       -> SHIMS (1-file lib.rs each)\nscripts/touring_premium_refactor_2026/w7_rewrite_crate_paths.py\n```\n\n## Next wave\n\nW8 (touring-hooks Internal Split) — depends on W4, W5, W6, W7 (all now done).\nW10 (touring-orchestration Fusion) should absorb touring-cortex (W6 deferral).\n"
